    {
      "id": "conditional-score",
      "source_ids": [
        "A3.E1"
      ],
      "role": "source-proof-ingredient",
      "statement": "For smooth compactly supported f, differentiate the normalized conditional density. Its score covariance is the derivative of Af. Conditional strong convexity, Hessian bounds and beta eta<=1 bound directional score variance; conditional Cauchy-Schwarz and integration yield C.2.",
      "literal_formula_alttexts": {
        "A3.E1": [
          "\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\\mathrm{Cov}\\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\\bigm|Y_{+}=y\\bigr)\\,."
        ]
      },
      "literal_byte_anchors": {
        "A3.E1": [
          {
            "math_id": "A3.E1.m1",
            "byte_start": 1008236,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 1009350,
            "raw_sha256": "09e683071db597f3c4165686d6e0d3cb663cc019c0d01a9006ddccc0e1029a94"
          }
        ]
      },
      "regularity": "The proof explicitly extends the smooth calculation to all L2 f by density and closedness of the gradient. Differentiation under the normalized integral, integrable score/covariance and conditional Poincare are required by this route and furnished by the stated C2/Hessian/Gaussian-tail setting."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2-gradient-leakage",
      "source_ids": [
        "A3.E2"
      ],
      "role": "required-source-proof-ingredient",
      "statement": "For every L2 f, eta ||grad Af||^2 <= (1-alpha eta)^2/[4(1+alpha eta)] ||Tf||^2. In particular Af in H1 and B.13 follows.",
      "literal_formula_alttexts": {
        "A3.E2": [
          "\\displaystyle\\eta\\,\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\leq\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^{2}}{4\\,(1+\\alpha\\eta)}\\,\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\,."
        ]
      },
      "literal_byte_anchors": {
        "A3.E2": [
          {
            "math_id": "A3.E2.m1",
            "byte_start": 1021945,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 1023458,
            "raw_sha256": "e46b872902562f2495a99c7a2cd2029ee2f8860f47a6c39d8d0909a159c8416b"
          }
        ]
      },
      "source_binders": [
        "f in L2(pi_eta^Y)"
      ],
      "not_public_extra_hypotheses": [
        "C.2 is an intermediate estimate proved from the source assumptions, not an extra source theorem premise."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "C3-centered-Poincare",
      "source_ids": [
        "A3.E3"
      ],
      "role": "required-source-proof-ingredient",
      "statement": "For f in HP0, A fixes constants and is self-adjoint, so Af is centered. Marginal Poincare gives ||Af||^2 <= (1/alpha+eta)||grad Af||^2.",
      "literal_formula_alttexts": {
        "A3.E3": [
          "\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}}(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f)\\leq\\Bigl(\\frac{1}{\\alpha}+\\eta\\Bigr)\\,\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\,."
        ]
      },
      "literal_byte_anchors": {
        "A3.E3": [
          {
            "math_id": "A3.E3.m1",
            "byte_start": 1027443,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 1028798,
            "raw_sha256": "7edc4491eba06ffdb3a6c682da4c0d333f94552b1f6b5d15163b594f7ee8e68f"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "C4-norm-contraction",
      "source_ids": [
        "A3.E4",
        "A2.E12"
      ],
      "role": "required-source-proof-ingredient",
      "statement": "Combining C.2/C.3 and ||Tf||^2=||f||^2-||Af||^2 gives ||Af|| <= rho_mac ||f|| on HP0, rho=(1-alpha eta)/(1+alpha eta). This endpoint includes alpha eta=1 without dividing by rho.",
      "literal_formula_alttexts": {
        "A3.E4": [
          "\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|\\leq\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\|f\\|=\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\,\\|f\\|\\,."
        ],
        "A2.E12": [
          "\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\coloneqq\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\gamma_{\\rm gap}\\coloneqq\\sqrt{1-\\rho_{\\rm mac}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,."
        ]
      },
      "literal_byte_anchors": {
        "A3.E4": [
          {
            "math_id": "A3.E4.m1",
            "byte_start": 1029970,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 1031133,
            "raw_sha256": "d8ac0789bd4d691319fbea05b54b57e3cc4424db36962c1257796780a4f100d2"
          }
        ],
        "A2.E12": [
          {
            "math_id": "A2.E12.m1",
            "byte_start": 775269,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 776608,
            "raw_sha256": "9905e9f217f502cb25f0d34745f831a303d95a84d654d90d2e42a9dc47d34413"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "B14-side-uniform-lower",
      "source_ids": [
        "A3.E5",
        "A3.E6",
        "A3.E7",
        "A2.E14"
      ],
      "role": "independent-side-branch-of-lemma-B1",
      "statement": "Exchangeability and Gaussian Poincare show <g,(I-A)g><=2 eta||grad g||^2; applying g=Af and B.13 yields (I-A)^2(I+2A)>=0 and Spec(A) subset [-1/2,1]. This proves the separate A>=-I/2 statement and is not necessary for the norm-to-root B15 edge.",
      "literal_formula_alttexts": {
        "A3.E5": [
          "\\displaystyle\\bigl\\langle g,(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})g\\bigr\\rangle",
          "\\displaystyle=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\bigl(g(Y_{+})-g(Y_{-})\\bigr)^{2}\\bigr]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{X}\\mathbb{E}_{Z}\\bigl[\\bigl(g(X+\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)-g(X-\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)\\bigr)^{2}\\bigr]\\,."
        ],
        "A3.E6": [
          "\\bigl\\langle g,(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})g\\bigr\\rangle\\leq 2\\eta\\,\\|\\nabla g\\|^{2}\\,."
        ],
        "A3.E7": [
          "(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})^{2}(I+2\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})\\succeq 0\\,."
        ],
        "A2.E14": [
          "\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\|\\leq\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{and}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,I\\hskip 20.00003pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,."
        ]
      },
      "literal_byte_anchors": {
        "A3.E5": [
          {
            "math_id": "A3.E5.m1",
            "byte_start": 1034438,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 1035141,
