    {
      "id": "centered-root-B15",
      "source_ids": [
        "A2.E15",
        "A2.E12"
      ],
      "role": "selected-source-conclusion",
      "statement": "On HP0, Gamma=(I-A^2)^(1/2) >= gamma_gap I in Loewner order, gamma_gap=sqrt(1-rho^2)=2 sqrt(alpha eta)/(1+alpha eta)>0.",
      "literal_formula_alttexts": {
        "A2.E15": [
          "\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}=(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\\succeq\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I\\hskip 20.00003pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,."
        ],
        "A2.E12": [
          "\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\coloneqq\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\gamma_{\\rm gap}\\coloneqq\\sqrt{1-\\rho_{\\rm mac}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,."
        ]
      },
      "literal_byte_anchors": {
        "A2.E15": [
          {
            "math_id": "A2.E15.m1",
            "byte_start": 784175,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 785371,
            "raw_sha256": "6358fac9054d2fc6d800079096ec3d1b56da3b3ff7ff3111bbdeb8d3125d9fa0"
          }
        ],
        "A2.E12": [
          {
            "math_id": "A2.E12.m1",
            "byte_start": 775269,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 776608,
            "raw_sha256": "9905e9f217f502cb25f0d34745f831a303d95a84d654d90d2e42a9dc47d34413"
          }
        ]
      },
      "exact_sense": "For every f in HP0, <f,(Gamma-gamma_gap I)f> >= 0. Gamma is a bounded linear operator on a real scalar-valued-L2 Hilbert space; gamma_gap is a scalar. This source conclusion is not merely a numerical norm-coercivity inequality.",
      "square-root_step": "Self-adjoint centered A and C.4 give I-A^2 >= (1-rho^2)I. Spectral positivity/monotonicity for the unique positive root then gives B.15.",
      "reducing_space": "A fixes constants and preserves centered space. Functional calculus preserves that reducing space; the restriction of the full positive root is the centered positive root."
    },
    {
      "id": "centered-inverse-B16",
      "source_ids": [
        "A2.E16"
      ],
      "role": "selected-source-conclusion",
      "statement": "Gamma is boundedly invertible on HP0. VperpP=T Gamma^(-1):HP0->Hperp, T=VperpP Gamma on HP0 and VperpP* VperpP=I_HP0.",
      "literal_formula_alttexts": {
        "A2.E16": [
          "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\,:\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\longrightarrow\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}}\\,."
        ]
      },
      "literal_byte_anchors": {
        "A2.E16": [
          {
            "math_id": "A2.E16.m1",
            "byte_start": 790765,
            "byte_end_exclusive": 793076,
            "raw_sha256": "e4f18034c8ed8792b4874b861748629ebb2839a41d78897340e2de1a4b6395c8"
          }
        ]
      },
      "inverse_contract": "Gamma^(-1) is a genuine bounded two-sided inverse on HP0, not just a scalar reciprocal, arbitrary supplied inverse, one-sided inverse, or inverse on the full macroscopic space.",
      "analytic_step": "The positive centered lower bound yields injectivity and closed range; self-adjointness gives dense range by orthogonal-complement/kernel duality, hence surjectivity and bounded inverse, with norm at most 1/gamma.",
      "polar_step": "For f,g in HP0, <T Gamma^-1 f,T Gamma^-1 g>=<Gamma Gamma^-1 f,Gamma Gamma^-1 g>=<f,g>; thus the normalized leakage is an isometry."
    }
  ],
