  "endpoint_legality": {
    "alpha_eta_one": "Allowed by 0<alpha<=beta and beta eta<=1; it forces alpha=beta=eta^-1, rho=0, gamma=1. C.4 gives centered A=0, hence centered Gamma=I; its inverse and normalized leakage remain legal. No division by rho or 1-alpha eta is needed.",
    "rank_zero_or_trivial_space": "No nontrivial-dimension or nonzero-rank premise appears in B15/B16. A trivial centered Hilbert space has the unique identity/inverse/isometry statements vacuously. Zero contraction A on a nontrivial centered space yields Gamma=I and is also legal; it does not mean leakage T is zero. A zero leakage T on a nontrivial centered space is incompatible with gamma>0.",
    "full_space_failure": "On full HP, A1=1, hence Gamma1=0. The nonzero constant vector prevents bounded invertibility there. A full-space inverse is not licensed by the source."
